\section{Propulsion State Vector}
The MK-22 propulsion state vector is
\[
\mathbf{X}_{\text{prop}} =
\begin{bmatrix}
\omega_{\text{prop}} \\
P_{\text{boost}} \\
T_{\text{exhaust}} \\
\dot{m}_{\text{fuel}} \\
L_{\text{aero}}
\end{bmatrix}.
\]

Propulsion dynamics evolve under
\[
\frac{d\omega_{\text{prop}}}{dt}
=
\frac{dL_{\text{aero}}}{L_{\text{aero}}},
\]
and
\[
\frac{d(\omega_{\text{prop}} P_{\text{boost}})}{dt}
=
\Phi_{\text{MK22}}(\mathbf{X}_{\text{prop}}).
\]

\section{Propulsion Gradient Tensor}
Define the propulsion gradient tensor:
\[
\mathbf{G}_{\text{prop}} =
\frac{\partial \mathbf{F}_{\text{prop}}}{\partial \mathbf{X}_{\text{prop}}},
\]
where $\mathbf{F}_{\text{prop}}$ is the propulsion force vector.

The tensor encodes sensitivity of thrust and aero-propulsive coupling:
\[
\mathbf{G}_{\text{prop}} =
\begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\partial F_{x}}{\partial \omega_{\text{prop}}} &
\frac{\partial F_{x}}{\partial P_{\text{boost}}} &
\cdots \\
\frac{\partial F_{y}}{\partial \omega_{\text{prop}}} &
\frac{\partial F_{y}}{\partial P_{\text{boost}}} &
\cdots
\end{bmatrix}.
\]

